# LAMMPS input for melamine-formaldehyde (MF) *crosslinked network*
# backmapping -- bakery-faithful protocol, adapted from the validated
# uncrosslinked example examples/melamine/large/in.melamine_bakery_faithful.lammps
# (ported from examples/pet/large/in.pet, validated 2026-07-28; see
# research/checkpoints.md and research/decisions/
# 2026-07-19-prefer-bakery-protocol-no-frozen-cg.md).
#
# Structure (identical to the uncrosslinked example, no Phase 0 minimize,
# continuous dt=1fs throughout):
#   Stage 1 -- CG+AT equilibration at lambda=0.
#   Stage 2 -- lambda ramp 0->1. fix backmap drives CG bead position via
#             its own COM-shift toward the AT center of mass.
#   Stage 3 -- AT production at lambda=1. CG beads keep NO independent
#             integrator or thermostat; their motion comes entirely from
#             fix backmap's COM-tracking, exactly as in the PET checkpoint
#             and the uncrosslinked melamine example.
#
# Force field (pair/bond/angle/dihedral_coeff below) is copied VERBATIM,
# not hand-retyped, from the current backmap-prep output
# (examples/melamine_network/large/in.melamine_network, generated by Task
# 5/5b's `backmap-prep build-hybrid` + `build` from the migrated native v2
# settings.yaml -- see the Task 5b report for the atom-ID cross-reference
# that confirmed the new crosslink bond/angle/dihedral LAMMPS types (5;
# 40/41/45; 11/12/13) carry real, nonzero, unit-converted parameters, and
# do NOT change their `backmap/harmonic at` / `backmap/ryckaert at` style
# -- that is the correct, always-on-at-lambda=1, real-chemistry style,
# confirmed correct by two independent reviews).
#
# Differences from the uncrosslinked example's skeleton that are purely
# mechanical (system-specific values regenerated by backmap-prep, not
# hand edits): atom/bond/angle/dihedral type COUNTS and VALUES (crosslink
# adds angle types 40/41/45 and dihedral types 11/12/13; atom-type LJ
# params differ because leaving-group atoms at reacted sites were removed,
# reshuffling backmap-prep's internal atom-type table); comm_modify cutoff
# (90.66, backmap-prep's own computed value for this larger crosslinked
# system, vs the uncrosslinked example's manually-bumped 90.00); pair_style
# backmap/lj/coul cutoffs (12.00/12.00/9.00 here vs 14.00/14.00/9.00 there,
# again backmap-prep's own system-specific values, not a protocol choice).
# bond_style/angle_style declarations also differ (no plain `harmonic`
# sub-style here -- every AT bond/angle in this network-engine-generated
# skeleton is tagged `backmap/harmonic at`, unlike the uncrosslinked
# example's mix of plain `harmonic` + `backmap/harmonic at`); this is a
# builder-code-path difference already reviewed and accepted in Task 5/5b,
# not something re-classified here -- copied as generated.
#
# CG-CG tabulated nonbonded potential: `pair_coeff 1 1 cg table_A_A.table
# ENTRY` below wires a real CG-CG tabulated potential, matching the
# uncrosslinked example's own `pair_coeff 1 1 cg table_A_A.table ENTRY`.
# table_A_A.xvg was vendored in this directory since Task 1 but, as
# originally generated (Task 6), this example's settings.yaml (native v2,
# `engine: network`) had no `simulation.table_groups` key, so
# backmap-prep's CG-CG pair-table wiring
# (python/src/backmap_prep/network/lammps_builder.py, `_resolve_pair_tables`
# around line 763: `table_groups = set(settings.simulation.table_groups);
# if not table_groups: return`) was a no-op, and every CG-CG pair fell
# through to the `cg 0.0 0.0` default in writers.py -- meaning there was NO
# CG-CG nonbonded interaction at all until Task 2c added `simulation:
# {table_groups: [A]}` to settings.yaml and regenerated the skeleton with
# the real table wired in (see the Task 2c report for the fix and its
# CG-CG-only verification against AT-level type IDs/counts).
#
# `fix pairs all backmap/pairs at file pairs.dat cut 12.000000` (below) has
# no counterpart in the uncrosslinked example: pairs.dat (Task 5b) encodes
# cross-molecule same-network-cluster nonbonded exclusion/scaling pairs
# that only exist because of crosslinking (special_bonds' molecule-local
# 1-2/1-3/1-4 exclusions cannot reach across a crosslink bond into a
# different original molecule). Kept from the skeleton as a structurally
# necessary, not optional, addition for this network topology.
#
# Velocity initialization: uses the generated skeleton's own
# `velocity all create` (not the uncrosslinked example's bakery-style
# shared CG+AT `read_dump ... melamine_vel.bakery.dump`, which requires
# running melamine_bakery_velocities.py against melamine_network.data to
# produce a new committed binary artifact -- out of scope for this
# single-file task; left for a follow-up if the Task 7 pilot run wants it).
#
# fix bm/fix cap/fix therm_at parameters (alpha=0.0001, lambda0=0.0,
# Langevin damp=33.3, capforce fmax=1195.03) are copied from the
# uncrosslinked example's validated protocol as the STARTING point for
# this crosslinked system -- NOT yet re-tuned here. Re-tuning, if needed,
# happens in Task 7's pilot run, not in this task.
#
# Usage:
#   lmp -in in.melamine_network_bakery_faithful.lammps \
#     -var eq_steps 10000 -var ramp_steps 10000 -var prod_steps 500000

variable eq_steps   index 2000
variable ramp_steps index 5000
variable prod_steps index 20000

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

read_data melamine_network.data
reset_atoms image all

# backmap-prep's own computed value for this system (see header note above
# on why this differs from the uncrosslinked example's manually-bumped
# 90.00): guarantees every atom of a molecule (CG bead + AT fragment, now
# possibly spanning a crosslink) stays visible to fix backmap regardless of
# MPI domain decomposition.
comm_modify cutoff 90.66

# lj/cut/coul/cut/ecap (not plain lj/cut/coul/cut, matching the
# uncrosslinked example's validated fix): same-CG-bead AT-AT pairs are
# always full-strength in pair_backmap regardless of lambda (by design --
# real intra-fragment chemistry). The 12.00/12.00/9.00 cutoffs and the
# final 14.00 table-region cutoff are copied unchanged from the generated
# in.melamine_network skeleton's own plain `lj/cut/coul/cut` pair_style
# line; only the sub-style name (+ecap) and the two extra ecap args
# (0.5, 5.0) are added, exactly as the uncrosslinked example added them to
# ITS skeleton's line. 4th arg (5.0 A) is the opt-in coul_cap_radius,
# caching the same flat-force/flat-energy treatment used for LJ, applied to
# Coulomb too, for r <= 5.0 A, to absorb transient same-bead strain during
# eq/ramp -- reissued to 0.0 (disabled) before Stage 3 below.
pair_style backmap 12.00 lj/cut/coul/cut/ecap 12.00 9.00 0.5 5.0 14.00 table linear 1000
pair_coeff 1 1 cg table_A_A.table ENTRY
pair_coeff 1 2 none
pair_coeff 1 3 none
pair_coeff 1 4 none
pair_coeff 1 5 none
pair_coeff 1 6 none
pair_coeff 1 7 none
pair_coeff 1 8 none
pair_coeff 1 9 none
pair_coeff 2 2 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 2 3 atomistic 0.109087 3.425000
pair_coeff 2 4 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 2 5 atomistic 0.105925 3.400000
pair_coeff 2 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.210000
pair_coeff 2 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.900000
pair_coeff 2 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 2 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 3 3 atomistic 0.070000 3.550000
pair_coeff 3 4 atomistic 0.109087 3.425000
pair_coeff 3 5 atomistic 0.067971 3.525000
pair_coeff 3 6 atomistic 0.109087 3.335000
pair_coeff 3 7 atomistic 0.045826 3.025000
pair_coeff 3 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 3 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 4 4 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 4 5 atomistic 0.105925 3.400000
pair_coeff 4 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.210000
pair_coeff 4 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.900000
pair_coeff 4 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 4 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 5 5 atomistic 0.066000 3.500000
pair_coeff 5 6 atomistic 0.105925 3.310000
pair_coeff 5 7 atomistic 0.044497 3.000000
pair_coeff 5 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 5 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 6 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.120000
pair_coeff 6 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.810000
pair_coeff 6 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 6 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 7 7 atomistic 0.030000 2.500000
pair_coeff 7 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 7 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 8 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 8 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 9 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000

bond_style hybrid backmap/harmonic backmap/table linear 1000
bond_coeff 1 backmap/harmonic at 481.000531 1.350000
bond_coeff 2 backmap/harmonic at 481.000531 1.370000
bond_coeff 3 backmap/harmonic at 382.000422 1.470000
bond_coeff 4 backmap/harmonic at 434.000479 1.010000
bond_coeff 5 backmap/harmonic at 320.000353 1.430000
bond_coeff 6 backmap/harmonic at 340.000375 1.100000
bond_coeff 7 backmap/harmonic at 553.000611 0.980000
bond_coeff 8 backmap/harmonic at 553.000611 0.970000
bond_coeff 9 backmap/table cg table_b1.table ENTRY
bond_coeff 10 backmap/harmonic at 481.000531 1.360000

angle_style backmap/harmonic
angle_coeff 1 at 80.000088 115.9740
angle_coeff 2 at 50.000055 122.7480
angle_coeff 3 at 35.000039 117.1410
angle_coeff 4 at 80.000088 112.2030
angle_coeff 5 at 35.000039 109.7990
angle_coeff 6 at 35.000039 110.3940
angle_coeff 7 at 35.000039 116.4310
angle_coeff 8 at 35.000039 107.8120
angle_coeff 9 at 35.000039 108.1410
angle_coeff 10 at 33.000036 108.3770
angle_coeff 11 at 80.000088 116.1820
angle_coeff 12 at 50.000055 123.0140
angle_coeff 13 at 35.000039 117.6650
angle_coeff 14 at 80.000088 112.1460
angle_coeff 15 at 35.000039 110.3040
angle_coeff 16 at 35.000039 109.9090
angle_coeff 17 at 35.000039 116.9500
angle_coeff 18 at 35.000039 108.1470
angle_coeff 19 at 35.000039 107.7610
angle_coeff 20 at 33.000036 108.4640
angle_coeff 21 at 80.000088 118.7940
angle_coeff 22 at 50.000055 123.0660
angle_coeff 23 at 35.000039 117.2970
angle_coeff 24 at 80.000088 112.5740
angle_coeff 25 at 35.000039 109.7450
angle_coeff 26 at 35.000039 110.2540
angle_coeff 27 at 35.000039 116.7990
angle_coeff 28 at 35.000039 107.8650
angle_coeff 29 at 35.000039 107.9800
angle_coeff 30 at 33.000036 108.2970
angle_coeff 31 at 55.000061 107.5770
angle_coeff 32 at 55.000061 108.8060
angle_coeff 33 at 55.000061 107.8310
angle_coeff 34 at 80.000088 125.2370
angle_coeff 35 at 80.000088 125.0100
angle_coeff 36 at 80.000088 116.1640
angle_coeff 37 at 40.000044 114.8070
angle_coeff 38 at 40.000044 114.8430
angle_coeff 39 at 80.000088 118.7880
angle_coeff 40 at 50.000055 109.5000
angle_coeff 41 at 35.000039 109.5000
angle_coeff 42 at 80.000088 124.9860
angle_coeff 43 at 40.000044 115.1170
angle_coeff 44 at 80.000088 118.8230
angle_coeff 45 at 60.000066 109.5000

dihedral_style hybrid ryckaert backmap/ryckaert
dihedral_coeff 1 ryckaert 7.936008 -0.000000 -7.936008 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 2 ryckaert 4.900005 -0.000000 -4.900005 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 3 ryckaert 6.089008 -0.000000 -6.089008 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 4 ryckaert 0.280000 -0.840001 0.000000 1.120001 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 5 ryckaert 0.200000 -0.600001 0.000000 0.800001 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 6 ryckaert 4.000004 -1.000001 -5.000006 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 7 ryckaert 0.225000 -0.675001 0.000000 0.900001 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 8 backmap/ryckaert at 7.239009 1.150001 -6.089008 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 9 backmap/ryckaert at 7.936008 -0.000000 -7.936008 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 10 backmap/ryckaert at 4.900005 -0.000000 -4.900005 -0.000000 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 11 backmap/ryckaert at 0.380000 -1.140001 0.000000 1.520002 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 12 backmap/ryckaert at 0.427500 -0.834499 0.128000 1.390002 0.000000 -0.000000
dihedral_coeff 13 backmap/ryckaert at -0.303000 -0.722001 0.417001 0.836000 0.000000 -0.000000

special_bonds lj 0.0 0.0 0.0 coul 0.0 0.0 0.0

group at_atoms type 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
group cg_atoms type 1

neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes

# Bakery-style shared CG+AT read_dump velocity file (as used by the
# uncrosslinked example) was not regenerated for this network variant --
# see header note. Using the generated skeleton's own initialization
# instead, as this pilot's starting point.
velocity all create 300.0 48279 dist gaussian mom yes rot yes

fix integrate_at at_atoms nve
fix therm_at at_atoms langevin 300.0 300.0 33.3 48279

fix bm all backmap cg_type 1 alpha 0.0001 lambda0 0.0
fix cap all backmap/capforce 1195.0300

# Crosslink-specific cross-molecule nonbonded exclusion/scaling pairs (see
# header note): no counterpart in the uncrosslinked example.
fix pairs all backmap/pairs at file pairs.dat cut 12.000000

# SHAKE on the explicit-hydrogen (X-H) bond types, same fix as PET's
# established resolution for the identical marginal-timestep failure mode
# (research/experiments/20260724_pet-water-lj-root-cause-and-fix.md,
# 20260723_pet-lambda0-shake-fix-order.md). Root-caused for this network
# example in research/experiments/20260808_melamine-network-pilot-eq-instability.md:
# bond type 4 (N-H, K=434.0 kcal/mol/A^2, r0=1.01 A) has a natural period
# of 10.11 fs, leaving dt=1fs almost no accuracy margin (T/10=1.011 fs);
# every crosslink-junction bead (90% of the system) additionally carries
# newly-extrapolated angle/dihedral parameters immediately adjacent to
# this bond (decisions/2026-08-06-mf-network-ether-ff-params.md) that
# pump resonant energy into it over ~150-200 steps -- confirmed via a
# fully deterministic (zero velocity, no Langevin, no CapForce) pure-NVE
# rerun that still diverged, ruling out any noise-based explanation.
# Declared AFTER bm/pairs/cap, matching PET's own established fix-order
# finding: SHAKE must see the complete final force (post CG->AT
# redistribution + CapForce clipping), not an incomplete picture.
fix shake_xh at_atoms shake 0.0001 20 0 b 4 6 7 8

fix_modify bm active no

compute at_temp at_atoms temp
compute cg_temp cg_atoms temp

thermo 500
thermo_style custom step temp c_at_temp c_cg_temp pe epair ebond eangle edihed f_bm f_cap f_cap[2]
thermo_modify colname f_bm lambda
thermo_modify colname f_cap ncapped
thermo_modify colname f_cap[2] Fobs
thermo_modify temp at_temp
thermo_modify lost ignore

dump traj at_atoms custom 1000 dump.at_network_prod id mol type x y z
dump_modify traj sort id

timestep 1.00

# --- Stage 1: lambda=0 equilibration (no Phase 0 minimize) ---
run ${eq_steps}
print "EQ done step=$(step) T=$(c_at_temp) Ebond=$(ebond) Eangle=$(eangle)"

# --- Stage 2: lambda ramp 0 -> 1 (continuous, no frozen-CG break) ---
fix_modify bm active yes
run ${ramp_steps}
print "RAMP done step=$(step) T=$(c_at_temp) lambda=$(f_bm) Ebond=$(ebond) Eangle=$(eangle)"

# --- Stage 3: lambda=1 production ---
# coul_cap_radius was only ever meant to absorb the transient step-0
# same-bead strain during eq/ramp, matching the uncrosslinked example's
# rationale exactly. Reissue pair_style with coul_cap_radius=0.0 (disabled)
# so production frames reflect full, uncapped Coulomb like any normal AT
# simulation. A new pair_style wipes all pair_coeff entries, so the full
# table below is byte-identical to the block above except the 4th
# pair_style arg (5.0 -> 0.0).
pair_style backmap 12.00 lj/cut/coul/cut/ecap 12.00 9.00 0.5 0.0 14.00 table linear 1000
pair_coeff 1 1 cg table_A_A.table ENTRY
pair_coeff 1 2 none
pair_coeff 1 3 none
pair_coeff 1 4 none
pair_coeff 1 5 none
pair_coeff 1 6 none
pair_coeff 1 7 none
pair_coeff 1 8 none
pair_coeff 1 9 none
pair_coeff 2 2 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 2 3 atomistic 0.109087 3.425000
pair_coeff 2 4 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 2 5 atomistic 0.105925 3.400000
pair_coeff 2 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.210000
pair_coeff 2 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.900000
pair_coeff 2 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 2 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 3 3 atomistic 0.070000 3.550000
pair_coeff 3 4 atomistic 0.109087 3.425000
pair_coeff 3 5 atomistic 0.067971 3.525000
pair_coeff 3 6 atomistic 0.109087 3.335000
pair_coeff 3 7 atomistic 0.045826 3.025000
pair_coeff 3 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 3 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 4 4 atomistic 0.170000 3.300000
pair_coeff 4 5 atomistic 0.105925 3.400000
pair_coeff 4 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.210000
pair_coeff 4 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.900000
pair_coeff 4 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 4 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 5 5 atomistic 0.066000 3.500000
pair_coeff 5 6 atomistic 0.105925 3.310000
pair_coeff 5 7 atomistic 0.044497 3.000000
pair_coeff 5 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 5 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 6 6 atomistic 0.170000 3.120000
pair_coeff 6 7 atomistic 0.071414 2.810000
pair_coeff 6 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 6 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 7 7 atomistic 0.030000 2.500000
pair_coeff 7 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 7 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 8 8 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 8 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
pair_coeff 9 9 atomistic 0.000000 0.000000
run ${prod_steps}
print "PRODUCTION done step=$(step) T=$(c_at_temp) lambda=$(f_bm) Ebond=$(ebond) Eangle=$(eangle)"

write_data melamine_network_hybrid_final.data
